From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yugidraft <yugidraft@localhost>
Date: Tue, 15 Feb 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] core: a Tag partner's turn counts as an own turn for
 RESET_SELF_TURN at n > 2

effect::reset(RESET_PHASE) took "own turn" as pid == turn player, but
"opponent turn" already meant another team. In Tag an effect of the partner
seat with RESET_SELF_TURN and RESET_OPPO_TURN (the default of RESET_PHASE
without a turn flag, so "until the end of this turn") was not counted in the
turn of the partner's own team when the turn player was the other seat of
that team. It stayed one turn too long. A disable-field effect registered by
the second seat of a team at the End Phase of the first seat's turn showed
it: the zone stayed disabled during the next turn.

At n > 2 own turn is now a turn of the own team (is_duelist and same_team).
In FFA every seat is its own team, so nothing changes there. n == 2 keeps
pid == turn player, the same bytes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UrYy4jjEcbJHKdcVYasfdb
---
 effect.cpp | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/effect.cpp b/effect.cpp
index 778d7a3..7859680 100644
--- a/effect.cpp
+++ b/effect.cpp
@@ -685,7 +685,9 @@ int32_t effect::reset(uint32_t reset_level, uint32_t reset_type) {
 		uint8_t tp = pduel->game_field->infos.turn_player;
 		const auto& gf = *pduel->game_field;
 		const bool oppo_turn = gf.n_duelists == 2 ? pid != tp : (gf.is_duelist(pid) && !gf.same_team(pid, tp));
-		if((((reset_flag & RESET_SELF_TURN) && pid == tp) || ((reset_flag & RESET_OPPO_TURN) && oppo_turn))
+		// at n > 2 "own turn" is a turn of the own team (the Tag partner's turn counts), as "opponent turn" already is
+		const bool self_turn = gf.n_duelists == 2 ? pid == tp : (gf.is_duelist(pid) && gf.same_team(pid, tp));
+		if((((reset_flag & RESET_SELF_TURN) && self_turn) || ((reset_flag & RESET_OPPO_TURN) && oppo_turn))
 				&& (reset_level & 0x3ff & reset_flag))
 			--reset_count;
 		if(reset_count == 0)
